# Helm charts of {{ topology.project_slug }}

Generated and kept current by forge (`deploy.helm_layout: per_service`). Each service is its own chart and its own
release, named after the service, so it rolls out, fails and rolls back alone, and its Service answers at
`http://<service>:<port>`, the URL its siblings already carry (`INTERNAL_SERVICE_URL_<NAME>`).

| Chart | Release | Holds |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `deploy/helm/platform` | `platform` | the Ingress to every service; the optional in-cluster Postgres, Redis, Keycloak and gatekeeper (`infra.inCluster`, dev/demo only) |
{%- for be in topology.backends %}
| `deploy/helm/{{ be.name }}` | `{{ be.name }}` | the {{ be.language }} backend: Deployment, Service on port {{ be.port }}, HPA, ConfigMap, Secret{{ ", migrate Job" if be.has_migrations }} |
{%- endfor %}
{%- for fe in topology.frontends %}
| `deploy/helm/{{ fe.name }}` | `{{ fe.name }}` | the {{ fe.app }} frontend: nginx serving the built SPA |
{%- endfor %}

Install the platform first, then the services (`make helm-install`), each with its environment's values:

    helm upgrade --install <chart> deploy/helm/<chart> -f deploy/helm/<chart>/values-<env>.yaml

Every `values.yaml` is forge-owned (re-rendered on `forge --update`, three-way merged); keep environment values in
separate files.
